{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967571-bodyguards-of-the-ultraelite","id":967571,"title":"Bodyguards of the Ultraelite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-11T15:45:27-07:00","id":967571,"title":"Bodyguards of the Ultraelite","content":"So, suppose that an Illuminati exists. A group of the most influential, rich and powerful people on earth.<br /> <br /> If you were to want to stalk these people, or god forbid wish them harm... who stops you?<br /> <br /> In a world saturated with the strange and enveloped in multiple overlapping supernatural communities, who protects and advises the 1%?<br /> <br /> Are they human? Are the people they guard, human?<br /> <br /> It's my birthday soon! And if I could ask for one thing, it would be help developing this idea. Anybody have any suggestions about various critters and tools that the rich and famous might employ to secure privacy and safety in a world gone mad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:47:45-07:00","id":967573,"title":"","content":"I could see a lodge of primarily Hunters in Darkness dedicating themselves to protecting certain people. Providing they were dangerous enough it would allow for an interesting variation in prey, as they hunt whoever is sent after the one they guard.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you do have the Seers who are basically the Mage 1%. I believe they have some sort of private soldier race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-11-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:20:22-07:00","id":967669,"title":"","content":"Seeing as they are basically the CoD illuminati, each hunter conspiracy and the more affluent compacts can afford their own protection within their organizations, as well as hiring out to others for such services as well in return for favors or blackmail material. Forces like TFV and the Ascending Ones probably even are willing to guard paranormal beings as well for a nice price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:21:14-07:00","id":967739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967571-bodyguards-of-the-ultraelite#post967571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, suppose that an Illuminati exists. A group of the most influential, rich and powerful people on earth.<br /> <br /> If you were to want to stalk these people, or god forbid wish them harm... who stops you?<br /> <br /> In a world saturated with the strange and enveloped in multiple overlapping supernatural communities, who protects and advises the 1%?<br /> <br /> Are they human? Are the people they guard, human?<br /> <br /> It's my birthday soon! And if I could ask for one thing, it would be help developing this idea. Anybody have any suggestions about various critters and tools that the rich and famous might employ to secure privacy and safety in a world gone mad?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends on who you're asking. Usually, it'd be thematically appropriate for who you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolf Shaman or Spirit Mage Powerful spirits!<br /> <br /> Vampire of the Order of Longinus? Elite vampire and ghoul &quot;Knights&quot;<br /> <br /> Business men? Best security money can buy! for TCG, Thaumatech armed Hunters of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:37:17-07:00","id":967750,"title":"","content":"Dogs of War opens things up to some interesting PMCs and security firms. There was one character who had a magical sword that allowed them to summon an army of ghosts. It's easy to imagine variants of such a thing with other ephemerals. I like the idea of a sort of 'Daern's Instant Fortress,' magical object. Not one that creates a castle, but one that creates servitors that guard, watch and otherwise protect the location you're in.<br /> <br /> There are some vampire disciplines that allow for a claiming of an area, which makes it easy to defend, but they tend to require a long habitation on the vampire's part.<br /> <br /> While not specifically about protecting a person, a pack of werewolves could make a structure or location basically impenetrable, even offering penalties to opening and flat out shutting down magical portals within them. Add some other Gifts like Shutdown or Garble, or the Gifts of Weather and if someone does manage to come through, you can make them severely regret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-12-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:34:52-07:00","id":967831,"title":"","content":"I mentioned this a while ago in the Hunter forum, but I could see Illuminati style conspiracies as another dark mirror to hunters.<br /> <br /> Hunter conspiracies have resources, including such things as magic, psychic powers, and advanced technology.<br /> <br /> But the nature of people in general and CofD in particular, I see no reason to think that there couldn't just as easily be hunter like conspiracies with very different goals than hunting monsters.<br /> So my inclination would be to take the hunter conspiracies and illuminate them.<br /> <br /> The doctor who came up with the wintergreen process could have just as easily sold it to those seeking to rule the world.<br /> <br /> If the Lucifuge exist, how about a group descended from the god kings of Egypt or the divine blood of the merovingians? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:33:40-07:00","id":968119,"title":"","content":"First they would not be ordinary humans. No matter how brilliant or lucky Warren Buffet may be he has had only one lifetime in which to amass his wealth, not enough time to compete with those who might have had centuries of acquisition. Even if he somehow did it some supernatural would take him in hand and make his wealth their own. If you insist on an exception perhaps the descendants of a trusted ghoul who's master was killed leaving him with control of the initial fortune and enough knowledge passed down to his heirs to avoid being ghouled again.<br /> \u200bSecond, their first defender would be that they aren't Warren Buffet. The true powers of the world would not be listed in Forbes Magazine, no one outside of a very limited circle would know who they are as all of their wealth would be hidden behind puppets and bureaucratic labyrinths. After that they would use whatever personnel is appropriate, with most having no clue who they are ultimately protecting. You can't betray what you don't know. It would be no mean feat for a five hundred year old Ventrue, much less a group like the Seers, to create their own version of a Hunter Conspiracy duped into protecting their interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:16:09-07:00","id":969174,"title":"","content":"If you're a Seer of the Great Ministries, you can have a bunch of Servitors, and in one of the books there was a Pylon that could get Thaumatechnology and Advanced Armory.<br /> <br /> If you're a Praetorian specifically, you can get a guard of Myrmidons, which are an engineered slave race of servitor Proximi that can do some Forces, Prime and Mind magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:35:15-07:00","id":969756,"title":"","content":"In fact, take this:<br /> <br /> <b>Myrmidon Bodyguard</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Sir, I would advise you to not step into that building without sufficient protection.<br /> <br /> No sir, I understand sir.<br /> <br /> For The Throne.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Description</b>: She wears a black suit with a clip-on tie and dark mirrorshades, she wears no body armour but she clearly trusts she doesn't need it. Her gait is professional and her movements are calculated and measured, whenever she speaks, she does so with a curt and professional voice.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4, Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>General Dice Pools</b>: Got Your Back 7, Let The Professionals Handle This 6, Won't Back Down 4<br /> <br /> <b>Combat Dice Pools</b>: Grappling 6, Guns 7, Combat Knives 7<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative Modifier</b>: +8<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 8<br /> <b>Health</b>: 9<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 3<br /> <b>Size</b>: 5<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 13<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings</b>: Nightvision (1), Invisibility (2), Turn Momentum (3), Mental Scan (1), Mental Shield (2), Supernal Vision (1).<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment</b>:<br /> <br /> Suit with Armor 3/3 immune to Armour Piercing.<br /> Light pistol with the damage of a rifle, 9-again of a shotgun, long bursts of an SMG and the range of a sniper. Because fuck you that's why.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Name</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Damage</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ranges</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Clip</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Initiative</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Str</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Size</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Mk1 SARISSA</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4 - 9-again</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">200/400/800</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> </table></div> Can perform long bursts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T05:58:11-07:00","id":969839,"title":"","content":"While I understand the arguments against mere mortals hiring powerful supernatural bodyguards, I wonder about the lesser templates. Could a wealthy stock trader hire a personal psychic to guard his brains? Or perhaps an heiress who grew up with the family thaumaturge and his apprentice. <br /> <br /> While less grand, minor supernatural movements provide a tie in for mortal and mortal+ games. Also major splat interaction if they cause a big enough stir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:22:11-07:00","id":970219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967571-bodyguards-of-the-ultraelite?p=969839#post969839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I understand the arguments against mere mortals hiring powerful supernatural bodyguards, I wonder about the lesser templates. Could a wealthy stock trader hire a personal psychic to guard his brains? Or perhaps an heiress who grew up with the family thaumaturge and his apprentice.<br /> <br /> While less grand, minor supernatural movements provide a tie in for mortal and mortal+ games. Also major splat interaction if they cause a big enough stir.</div> </div> </div> </div>He totally could hire a personal psychic or a thaumaturge.<br /> <br /> I'm generally of the opinion that mortals in CofD are never 'mere'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}